    <item>
      <title>Books</title>
      <link>https://janeetbajracharya.com.np/books/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 30 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://janeetbajracharya.com.np/books/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;A general goal of mine is to read more books! Here is a list of books that I have read in recent memory (since 2025):&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;2025&#34;&gt;2025:&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(In Progress) Status and Culture - W. David Marx&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Part of my reflections on taste, and performativity.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(In Progress) Hard to be a God - Arkady and Boris Strugatsky&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Watched a movie with a professor and friends, ended up being a pretty explicit and gnarly movie. However, the story always seemed appealing.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;If Beale Street Could Talk - James Baldwin&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Careless People - Sarah Wynn-Williams&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&amp;ldquo;Everyone is doing immoral things but me&amp;rdquo;. But an interesting account of what is going on from the top of the mountain.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Everything is Tuberculosis - John Green&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Video by &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/@acollierastro&#34;&gt;Angela Collier&lt;/a&gt; was the reason I listened to this book.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The Woman in the Dunes - Kobo Abe&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Watched the Criterion Collection movie of this and was inspired enough to read the book.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Suffocating.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The Art Doing of Science and Engineering - Richard Hamming&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Pachinko - Min Jin Lee&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Weapons of Math Destruction - Cathy O&amp;rsquo;Neil&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
